WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Type III covers low-pressure chillers. These are commercial systems — big
equipment, big consequences.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
EPA 608 Type III practice exam covering low-pressure system operation, recovery
requirements, purge units, water contamination, rupture discs, and
chiller-specific safety. 25 questions, 70 percent to pass.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Type III completes your Universal
certification when combined with Core, Type I, and Type II.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Know recovery levels for low-pressure systems. And — Know
purge unit function

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Why does a low-pressure system have air leaking in rather than refrigerant
leaking out? Think about the pressure relationship.

